        "headline": "Frost Advisory issued June 8 at 8:59AM AKDT until June 9 at 9:00AM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Temperatures as low as 34 could result in frost formation.\n\n* WHERE...Goldstream and Fairbanks.\n\n* WHEN...From 2 AM to 9 AM AKDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Frost could harm sensitive outdoor vegetation. Sensitive\noutdoor plants may be killed if left uncovered.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Temperatures drop into the low to mid 30s\ntonight as skies clear after midnight. Isolated locations in\ntypical cold spots may have frost tonight, specifically Goldstream\nValley. In the City of Fairbanks, frost i",
        "severity": "Minor",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
